nal calls for restraint. Their respective allies have the potential to catapult the conflict into a regional war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Macron and Steinmeier struggle to revive Franco-German ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a78ae118b99bb425d6b77341bbbb18ecd28b75ad5f1bf90f4f5bd71c9269bf3d</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635--64b747b714b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Presidents Frank-Walter Steinmeier and Emmanuel Macron are about to step down from their offices. Their meeting in France made it clear how urgently the Franco-German partnership needs new momentum.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af4ab47e711a9ae96f95fb95f26329ca2e3eb5b195a2c5bd26be0fdc7554dfa4</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>US imposes sanctions aiming to 'dismantle' International Criminal Court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b0b9584aaf2d95b9c8dd7eda1e686f4f5f8fedd6b43968d51f0df355f9c89e5</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-imposes-sanctions-aiming-to-dismantle-international-criminal-court/a-79618577--3c15e900b5b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-imposes-sanctions-aiming-to-dismantle-international-criminal-court/a-79618577?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has announced new sanctions on the International Criminal Court. It's the latest in a series of steps by the Donald Trump administration as it seeks to "dismantle" the intergovernmental organization.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi coalition vows 'firm' response after airport attack kills 3</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51195c2b46c6e54248410204c1ee1b1479182006291e253d501fa4534ee5d69b</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-coalition-vows-firm-response-after-airport-attack-kills-3/a-79615437--46e08f9efd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-coalition-vows-firm-response-after-airport-attack-kills-3/a-79615437?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia and its allied forces in Yemen vowed a "firm response" to Houthi attacks that target civilians. The kingdom's authorities said three Saudi nationals were killed in Thursday's attack on Riyadh airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is China seeking to restrict Taiwan's cultural presence?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:384347b0fdd8946d1a8a196cd537f253f789057980ea8fee4357601de73b9b71</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947--71784c91bb83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From coffee competitions to literature awards, Beijing appears to be working to limit Taiwan's international cultural and political impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9fe52a4a24015d6bda7630994a681f873021adfdcc2372ffdf5dd655df2314b</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Lifeline for Ukrainian refugees confronts donor fatigue and online abuse as anti-Ukrainian sentiment grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03eea21cf53965d0db36974c412e9e0e79cbb608156a32d8469b6ed2c02e3b7a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-se/a-79613292--19cba8c4d4f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-sentiment-grows/a-79613292?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian woman who fled the war in her country built a lifeline for refugees in Poland. Now her organization faces donor fatigue, funding cuts and rising hostility as support for Ukrainians in Poland wanes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's 'cockroaches' vs Election Commission: What you need to know ahead of CJP's October 10 protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0cc96794847dd9103bf87a64777df2a20ec29e2f701a1ab42b9c7a4d118a95e</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-cockroaches-vs-election-commission-what-you-need-to-know-ahead-of-cjp-s-october-10-protests/a-79608760--fa9a4a7bb711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-cockroaches-vs-election-commission-what-you-need-to-know-ahead-of-cjp-s-october-10-protests/a-79608760?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Indian capital New Delhi has been turned into a fortress with train and metro cancelations, barricades and heavy police presence ahead of Saturday's planned protests against the chief of India's electoral body.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hurricane Isaias intensifies en route to US Gulf Coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f59421d8b8bf7452b8a394aab76175f1f291f35310e4b17d79a8010eb8533750</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hurricane-isaias-intensifies-en-route-to-us-gulf-coast/a-79612756--4e23d2ef7c5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hurricane-isaias-intensifies-en-route-to-us-gulf-coast/a-79612756?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oil and gas production in the Gulf of Mexico has already been affected by the approaching hurricane, which has strengthened so far to Category 2.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ac4e7541e59dbe32e0b7e61bae89a431b2fd0c001b6326d316d5dee5e72656a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:43:00Z</published><li