on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551--518c4a71824f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Just hours before Lionel Messi played his last match for Argentina, Cristiano Ronaldo posted his latest salvo in a row with Portugal. Ronaldo wants to play on despite the troubles, while Messi bathed in adulation.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nobelitis — How winning a Nobel Prize can give you delusions of grandeur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4f3265b608d51a6a55d07e88ad117f8f8d7b0b7cae36286fa96f05f4ab919</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772--1ee420badedc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After being chosen for one of the world's most prestigious awards, some Nobel laureates lose touch with reality and suddenly start spouting unscientific nonsense. They're afflicted by what some have called "Nobelitis."</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Emerging economies are embracing solar power and skipping fossil fuels much faster than Europe or the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1fc38297532a7978aceeb1d4b27703dc858bfea58683b755693a131631924db</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-th/a-79474847--a24cf177c41d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-the-us/a-79474847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47c288d4f0ccaea0d360d72ea51c961f2396db7f3dba3fffca21fdca8d820d9a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ae4826da172f9261dd5891695714abcb41f53c9c861d81b362b6aedfbdcc043</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany shaken by espionage and treason allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b47556392401828cafe4081fa5ca7ff9939dffb7272ccb0cb6e69830d8aed064</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578--c39cf46fd6f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks ways to make expansion more palatable to members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d842d76e1682fcb73c7699828a671b533b13dbf710804d8c9567ce0b711abf10</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297--4cde5d079d87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has put forward ideas it hopes will both ease the EU expansion process and allay concerns among existing members. Several countries, not least war-torn Ukraine, are among the candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's conundrum: How to cut spending amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c807e11cb616baf871f343ee466e8a6bb08a002d743abae3d9bec4488757363c</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475--ca64b77315f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Lecornu is pledging to improve schools at a time when the government seeks to save billions. France's dilemma can be seen across the EU: How to cut spending when citizens are demanding more from the state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c37d5cd1a5bac594fe441b11a50a5c9383782e70f1ac92462ecd201eef35004b</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD makes history again in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a28b0200bb102bed8398022b7fb55ca1047ddbc2cf9ab3cb5a68099a457dc72</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146--3b11bbf1dc05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since the end of World War II, a German state parliament has chosen parliamentary speaker from the far right: Tobias Rausch of the Alternative for Germany (AfD).</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Literature Prize: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f99ce1f0b02de4aaa52675a689fbd1f6cb388abb8155116f80db894fdd61890e</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--42983d639d88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in Literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading claims spark plague fears in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2be955fb63cd4bb843a06ffec6902f4c3f40a32ac9ea799332d21c86bb7d621</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752--eaca60a52c9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of a lab worker at a plague research institute in Russia has sparked claims about a lab accident, hundreds of infections and international spread. Some of these viral narratives are misleading.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>AI models keep hacking real systems during tests. What does this mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9da90a1a220ffba847fce7aba8967343af57a61000e091e632533b9ee1c1edc1</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943--07f5722af213.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-models-keep-hacking-real-systems-during-tests-what-does-this-mean/a-79471943?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI models have repeatedly broken into real commercial and government systems during safety tests during 2026. Cybersecurity researcher Thorsten Holz explains what that means, and why he isn't expecting a robot uprising.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces a triple threat from Russia, China and domestic far-right extremists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94570b51bf3c7de64080565e57987ba636f990bc3ba0f81cd162d6b8c3681aa6</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-a-triple-threat-from-russia-china-and-domestic-far-right-extremists/a-79560490--8059184d93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-a-triple-threat-from-russia-china-and-domestic-far-right-extremists/a-79560490?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a rare public hearing Germany's intelligence agencies identified Russia as the country's most dangerous adversary. The threat from China is also coming into focus. And the homegrown far right also poses a challenge.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Far-right AfD gets first house speaker in a German state parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0eb194b9a7f700352e412092c9f520651b929feb808f633fbd22bc6144e4140</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497--5fb1cf58f705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since World War II, a far-right party has a house speaker in a German state parliament. And Germany's foreign minister has warned that the climate crisis could fuel extremism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ee16ff86d9ece07d6c291b50a6d6be6161092ad9ee03b7175607644f6d69aa3</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australia, New Zealand probe Flydubai pilot's time there</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8739eef1fb8a92128e64f2fd9cba3a66da00a6bf907f815956f4a51d294d3a38</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-new-zealand-probe-flydubai-pilot-s-time-there/a-79551423--4e0d79ffea0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-new-zealand-probe-flydubai-pilot-s-time-there/a-79551423?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Flydubai pilot from Oman suspected of trying to crash a plane in Israel spent time in Oceania as a young man. Police in both Australia and New Zealand said they would investigate his links to the countries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Euro plummets against US dollar: Has the next financial crisis begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd601e06d1491c77b6c57034e086864eee3fa432b203b4f4e4d2365f095e1520</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031--86ee12acb8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The euro has fallen to a 17-month low against the dollar. That will make inflation worse in the EU, where political worries and concern over French debt are already troubling investors. Is a fiscal crisis at hand?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trust in the German Constitutional Court is eroding — how can this be stopped?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e36e965fd498a94d73793d8b34d844887dc6cbbcd10ac8eb0007057e8ae440c6</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211--cc048545c82f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's top court, which turned 75 this year, is losing the population's trust, surveys show. Some say reforms in the way it picks candidates would help, to also accept candidates nominated by the far-right AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Spy chief warns Russia conflict risk growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73373ea8d31482734e6772daa6136528c5ab1b013844047e97f38d88810b78be</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789--3bde17a9e96c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is already waging a "shadow war" against Europe, the head of Germany's foreign intelligence service says. The Left Party is taking a case over remarks by the CDU's Katherina Reiche to a top court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp faces myriad of issues after rough start with Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4a1d950e70153cbcd82376860cdff8a59e02a822e15eeee647c0ce3d38539db</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-faces-myriad-of-issues-after-rough-start-with-germany/a-79547308--c13c1fe885bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-faces-myriad-of-issues-after-rough-start-with-germany/a-79547308?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp has done things a little differently since becoming Germany coach. Casting a wider net for talent and trying to connect with players and country haven't made an immediate impact, but he is not bowed.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia election: New steps to prevent electoral fraud, but nationalist parties remain on top</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28fa5c569328737045cab4a7de723f77767a616a4902f3c34b893125515d67c2</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="a