s, institutions and the public to make a push for solar power before the decade is out, repowering the world with cheap, clean energy. Is that possible?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc2f4e75352184c06cbe59c81753e6cdbfde354cbfc59359cefe94088e5c1df9</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City has become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>ARD-Deutschlandtrend survey: Germans unite in frustration over the government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5b671676a60aaa8a1c172999547d6201f0bd077b07ab0b0e72e42b720732828</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172--1741214668c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ard-deutschlandtrend-survey-germans-unite-in-frustration-over-the-government/a-79515172?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the 36th anniversary of reunification, Germans are dissatisfied with the country's political leaders. They don't believe they'll be able to handle the challenges posed by AI, Russia and Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Stock market scandal hits half a million investors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebcca026235c96e210ba0d9705f3d06e2b8de1c28786efd771f802df1c421ad5</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710--a0311f00dcbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Asset managers are alleged to have artificially inflated the value of their funds. Turkish authorities have made multiple arrests, and a leading AKP lawmaker has resigned.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wins first game as Germany coach, without 'top dogs'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c0a4939879bf49e0f07ddcf0cb9f30b4fce128e97cb7336b9a97027d56d037c</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898--6c1fca750e8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wins-first-game-as-germany-coach-without-top-dogs/a-79508898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It may have taken a little longer than he would have liked, but Jürgen Klopp has finally won a game as Germany coach. Despite a number of debutants, it was a familiar face who stood out in the victory over Serbia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could see drivers pay higher running costs while also increasing carbon emissions.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1ef4fbc040be22dacde732827d77ccf78517900af57bb03b617dff4d80665a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T11:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-/a-79496554--0804b7619722.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-costs-while-also-increasing-carbon-emissions/a-79496554?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could yet see drivers pay higher running costs while increasing planet-heating emissions.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germans' biggest fear is the high cost of living, an annual study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb69a0260329f4a7a0e488d5fb02a17e0600f8496ca752e6a76f79a06b9c88de</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762--40495e454721.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What do Germans fear most in 2026? Wars? Global crises? Wrong. Their biggest concern is the cost of living, which keeps rising.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz lauds NATO with Westphalian Peace Prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c6fe3b6e0aed5e82f60c7fac7d284d78e563857f91325e86a2aaa527ff8e583</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-lauds-nato-with-westphalian-peace-prize/live-79496180--2a3d5eea8753.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-lauds-nato-with-westphalian-peace-prize/live-79496180?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a ceremony to honor