9T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:215149488582d30ce9a491d8c48b614c46c5dd61ee2d901b1c71ff5c86b7cb4e</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97904dfaa4bf8b1e1a38d5b60a8d487215936176644386adeae7cfa0c28b494b</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Volkswagen ends collective wage agreements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eab2725eca841d9dab87a765b4276a814196757f8980ba858ac1b29c01d0e60d</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802--2228595954e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-ends-collective-wage-agreements/live-79481802?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an effort to cut costs, automaker Volkswagen terminated most of its collective wage agreements in Germany. This could reignite disputes with employee representatives.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino is a 'postcard from the future' — and could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4560c5665c22c6ceee76c1033a06c689b295038438190401876976b21d2a3adb</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945--e1a2336874a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-is-a-postcard-from-the-future-and-could-cause-451-000-excess-heat-deaths/a-79430945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The current El Nino could cause 451,000 excess heat deaths. Researchers warn it offers a glimpse of temperatures that may become normal within 20 years.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>South Park satirist pushes for accountability in Cornell gang-rape lawsuit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27ab0938deb5ab5057c53a82e19d21ae5acc3d4829d9da4149eb1a095719da93</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382--e2bb4e991ce2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Writer Toby Morton is using a new website to amplify allegations in a high-profile sexual assault lawsuit involving seven Cornell students. The reopening of the case is causing an outcry on social media.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6787f87035fd567baf07d101deb587be8edadd8772eeb003295dc6b51dd91ec2</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643--538fe77d9a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past six years, COVID, two wars and Donald Trump's tariffs have shaken world trade. With globalization already stalling, is this a temporary shock or the start of a great reversal?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>AI: Concern as Germany plans to double data center capacity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a85d1dda1d6debaae0e27e8c57a3b5450395494aa6dc48ad9cd312927dcc9e2</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-concern-as-germany-plans-to-double-data-center-capacity/a-79407981--ddf2b388dfde.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-concern-as-germany-plans-to-double-data-center-capacity/a-79407981?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is rewriting the rules to attract data center investment from AI companies. But local communities are becoming increasingly skeptical.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Spain grows fruit and vegetables for Europe, but it's running out of water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da120504125940a2f808805887734780628842d7b5687dfea7f8219e45372a18</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905--7611f918b844.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-grows-fruit-and-vegetables-for-europe-but-it-s-running-out-of-water/a-79399905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's southern coast produces up to 25% of Europe's fruit and vegetables. But amid intensive farming, climate change and illegal wells, the water it takes to grow them is drying up.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>What do Manchester City's charges mean for German football?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32294c273c21fdb7c40af21500d79b66bca8d1e4e758bf8a67ffe4537007089e</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412--ba8ebfa60874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manchester City have reportedly been found guilty of major financial rule breaches. What does this mean for German football?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Diesel prices are surging putting further pressure on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4e074813b39962da095dec7af1e9ef472fdde8fdb23ef2c5611cfae4f29a867</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992--edb37306aa00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/diesel-prices-are-surging-putting-further-pressure-on-europe/a-79390992?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trucks, farms and industry are powered with diesel. Now prices are soaring due to refinery disruptions, supply shortages and geopolitical tensions. A potential US export ban could make Europe's diesel crunch even worse.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Will Jürgen Klopp's charisma be enough for Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0acf3a3cacca84e01423929cf7c5c2909532fa22da7eed32841a6698ca9fae</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-j_rgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266--fed309f9f1f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-jürgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After defeat to Greece, Jürgen Klopp faces the first real test of his tenure as coach of Germany's national men's football team. Can his charisma alone push this group forward?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland beat Israel 3-0 in Nations League match overshadowed by political controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1267253d3137e9b227f61790d66bbdb0289683cb969ce5ab274b45a43ea75c47</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254--ac737f0c12b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ireland easily beat Israel in a Nations League fixture that 24 hours earlier appeared in doubt. One Irish player pulled out of the match to express his opposition to Israel's actions in the Gaza Strip.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What would Francis of Assisi make of his fame today?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73b8422c9fd2aa9dc7307a38e852c90cdad8e4db86dbbd5fa4ae56b0cfead0e2</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T06:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-francis-of-assisi-make-of-his-fame-today/a-79346151--db42471ab90e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-francis-of-assisi-make-of-his-fame-today/a-79346151?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Catholic saint renounced wealth and fame to become a mendicant friar. Yet throughout history, his teachings and life have inspired popes, Dante and even Mussolini.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash over data centers tests Europe's AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ddcde74c82a73dbf75da70d13400fd2c98135f0b880a28968647d0a7322ab85</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800--224361aa983d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive data centers needed to run AI are triggering protests across Europe. Their operators counter that they boost digital sovereignty and energy independence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>DW shows solidarity with Georgians' commitment to democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41b2e866a3b2f6beeef993d5b0ad1e9dcb597436a0fc1f31abcb007c1c257af5</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-shows-solidarity-with-georgians-commitment-to-democracy/a-79432731--f6945c635292.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-shows-solidarity-with-georgians-commitment-to-democracy/a-79432731?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cultural and media professionals in Georgia remain under threat. A DW panel brings together insiders who share their hopes and fears.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bundesliga, other top European leagues call for major FIFA reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e27de098ada8de987cd5e42807cba93ef738884c407fff6b5515b67b5fdd4ceb</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717--3029f0ff55b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundesliga and three other leading European football leagues have said major reforms to world-governing body FIFA are "essential." However, they stopped short of calling for the resignation of boss Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffff30ea64415990be67f46843361dc3355000d1215bf9f4e7e433e5f6a0fffd</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00b1c0565d047241e68794c4dd6cf9c104e42672929b33560104f20087b18f5a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Political psychology: Why extremist parties are thriving and what democratic politicians can do against it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:314f2bc6c20a1a569abb5bcc55c730ebbbc254d2dabdf39241d61b1139638330</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/political-psychology-why-extremist-parties-are-thriving-and-what-democratic-politicians-can-do-again/a-79410960--440643795892.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/political-psychology-why-extremist-parties-are-thriving-and-what-democratic-politicians-can-do-against-it/a-79410960?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right and far-left parties are celebrating success after success, leaving moderate politicians in the dust and worrying many Germans. Political psychology helps us understand what's behind growing polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Could flattering AI make humanity turn on itself?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8347d346899a7978b591529abce9ccdeb52c8f1b59047fe1a0a1040061f549c9</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-flattering-ai-make-humanity-turn-on-itself/a-79377894--285f77843c72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-flattering-ai-make-humanity-turn-on-itself/a-79377894?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A study shows chatbots mirror users' politics, part of a broader tendency known as AI sycophancy. Researchers fear this could deepen polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>China's 13-year-old swimming star raises questions on child athletes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ffc2d573cd23aae2b3fb90b8a2cf3d015b9b31afdc35ed4705bbad408af5722</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183--95db71a677f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three gold medals and three Asian Games records have catapulted China's Yu Zidi, 13, into the sporting spotlight. She is far from the first teen prodigy, but should teens be competing at elite level?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Munich and Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr – Germany's two remaining Olympic candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ecd5a3d348cee428cb37f967f2d7af515b19a94a11dfbe96106ac438b199d3</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-and-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-two-remaining-olympic-candidates/a-79386915--bae1fd64c3bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-and-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-two-remaining-olympic-candidates/a-79386915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich or the Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr region? Germany aims to host the Olympic Games again. Just two candidates are left after Berlin pulled out at the last minute.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino explained: How the weather pattern affects hurricanes and tropical storms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0be905f915569229fc7902d1840c4c8a22183180b3b6ced717a116ad72fa971a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511--be7cc5c8c0e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From drought to major floods and extreme heat, El Nino will have a huge impact on the world's weather. In the Atlantic, it could mean a season without hurricanes.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>China's new travel rules unsettle tech giants and talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46a1f4b42d3e1635c1788b29121cd5ed9d0703f617a24f98cfba14595cca030c</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937--16d904ca4025.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing is locking the gates to stop expertise and capital in strategic industries from fleeing. The country accused of industrial-scale intellectual property theft now fears the West will take its own.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Living in the shadow of LA's hidden oil wells</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b87d0a56546acf2d8c949c3b7b2fb1b6104c28f77ac70f22006ab9dfc1182a03</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T13:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/living-in-the-shadow-of-la-s-hidden-oil-wells/a-79237420--13c7836e2425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/living-in-the-shadow-of-la-s-hidden-oil-wells/a-79237420?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many lifelong residents of Los Angeles have health impacts from growing up close to oil extraction. Now, the city is trying to close down the worst offenders, but it's an enormous task.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Could we see MMA at the Olympics?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d33c9e1cb7261c7f586006a4afde918ff97dc51aa32834712fd728ebc889bfc</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605--f76e8af14c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mixed martial arts has made its debut at the Asian Games this week. It takes the sport closer to the Olympics, but there are doubts about the next step — and the influence of the popular and lucrative UFC.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Male infertility is 'grossly underreported'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be098fe8fb7276d6ce76456311ff41a0825505521d38c2389d6ed9053058caf9</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722--14a06576edd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's not all on women anymore — doctors do test men for sperm count and motility. But still too few men get checked, possibly due to a misconception that a healthy sex life means healthy sperm. Spoiler: It doesn't.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Will Germany have enough gas this winter amid energy supply crunch?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5176e1b2688923cb811f190de6b330558e02e2740faf7e6cc6862f906530f5d</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317--cfd94c55c93d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-germany-have-enough-gas-this-winter-amid-energy-supply-crunch/a-79360317?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage sites are far less full than in recent years. Officials say supplies are secure, but analysts warn that a cold winter or import disruptions could push prices higher. So how secure is the supply?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Princess Diana's brother makes explosive claims about royals in new memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d395ee42fd453667784e292fd314a7ed21d45c7426977f9f6cfadf6bb3c93358</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465--3d900d102240.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/princess-diana-s-brother-makes-explosive-claims-about-royals-in-new-memoir/a-79309465?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Here are some of the key revelations from Charles Earl Spencer's highly anticipated memoir "Swan Song: Diana, My Sister." It has already provoked Buckingham Palace to react.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's car crisis: Can the 35-hour workweek survive?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d38c45a96542605fac2ee0cd8b7e8f381ef45c49d07c8ef98c6621ff24ff8ad2</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488--cb2e3220b33e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-car-crisis-can-the-35-hour-workweek-survive/a-79307488?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German carmakers want employees to work 40 hours instead of the current 35 without extra pay, arguing it would improve competitiveness. Unions strongly oppose the proposal and view it as an attack on workers' rights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9755d39710fc28bf53e48f48d6e8b707f1d8c1b337d052ef9cd95046356342d7</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue for the government. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Summer of 2026 broke records in Europe, and caused deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fa1d1f82c17ca9e3ac7319095dc9884f0a265bdf3cf68cef5d9cde6284ce0a1</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T19:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630--5efe97f5474b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summer of 2026 was not only the hottest on record in Europe, it also saw a record number of people die. More than 16,000 are thought to have died because of the heat in Germany alone.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c8ac6e21a14196946084ac027ac1ab556095261f5e2cb3d72402cef5a61a7ec</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Rebels, workers, radicals: The making of 'Red Berlin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbceeff11d2703d69c2b6bbc4079877a81e021f23a20a76d52bd2457cbcefbed</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410--afcfe0d2ce3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bloody May, student sit-ins and the squatter movement: Berlin has long been a hotbed for working-class organizing and radical left-wing politics.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5ea10f43316743f98511babd761d8e3d4895445a968d33513bb342b953aa6ac</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz attacks spill oil into Persian Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19d6140c91c3e224d977291a5cd5b7d18cce82acae8149d025a3015b3c06cead</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092--09836173253c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As war disrupts one of the world's busiest shipping lanes, satellite images reveal that oil is spreading toward protected coral reefs and mangrove forests.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Dual citizenship means Germany now in competition for talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0537129a1a04fb2bfbc4497964f14a0827b2bf0ad86f39b773c4aed178eff4b5</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797--d43696518a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coach Jürgen Klopp has named several players to his first Germany squad who are eligible to play for other countries. Some still aren't committed to playing for thje national team long-term.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Beethoven and Andy Warhol: Rebel icons on show in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d0e11fd1940a0da2ce3a14a8920938fb6a4e4ac4696d383360bc2eee764e6e7</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944--59ad6d6535a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new exhibition "Beethoven by Warhol" at the Beethoven House in Bonn presents the pop artist's late masterpiece: a picture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e0298b1f33e7ad2dbb604d79367a5bb28c2e082cde2b3da1e3bf3808b648f8</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab4c46c5606767961d04084a8c3a48ae92f8a588705857c417c40b18a55547aa</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jews once lived lived here: When houses tell stories</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d00d9d0a57da268e33acf0af1ebc1c1e88e01f7dc7231ca362b0adfcbaf2450d</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jews-once-lived-lived-here-when-houses-tell-stories/a-79264813--f29d1ad1c32d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jews-once-lived-lived-here-when-houses-tell-stories/a-79264813?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Time and again, residents tracing the history of their homes discover the lives of Jewish predecessors who fled or were deported amid stories of suffering and loss.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Saint, sinner or feminist icon: How Mary Magdalene's image evolved through time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64bc2f4620bf48c3d9f939af720b041b751f5ba73731e6d50e2d2cd3e374f0ef</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868--1a6f3ade345e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From "Apostle of the Apostles" to prostitute, Mary Magdalene has been assigned a wide variety of roles, as a new exhibition shows.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change worsened Nepal's deadly mountain collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d2d8dfa92bb49a1d6dd0c2617587934c640d1bca9718c67e75c1b3e4d84e8fd</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578--691d9083ccec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A glacier and rock collapse in Nepal killed nearly 1,400 people and left thousands missing. Scientists say decades of warming helped set the disaster in motion.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13ad7ce0d12fc9a8d48e73ba641911b1c71b25914830df0b832e893b03aad2b7</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>German drama 'Blindspot Berlin' revisits 2016 Christmas market attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6831b5623e4804d424fd45349a3831ff1fa2ff12c27663b6c24b07924229e920</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162--11e3e3b69ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the terrorist attack on a Berlin Christmas market, a new German miniseries looks into the institutional failures that allowed the deadly truck rampage to happen.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How extreme heat is hitting wallets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c99b8888747505710a463cc423f37fa0a7cfa16019cc04236fee0fa4c36aeef2</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-hotter-weather-is-making-us-poorer/a-79268306--10853d8a0a0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-extreme-heat-is-hitting-wallets/a-79268306?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heat waves, wildfires and floods have cascading economic impacts, causing incomes to decline and the price of basic goods to rise. The trend will escalate as temperatures continue to increase.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish scientists find first evidence of Diplodocus dinosaur in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86db5eefaaa473614ecd5e7c95091233acfb03c5ea8281a3b2b6a4bdf49535c9</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825--f2d2e7bb0613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-scientists-find-first-evidence-of-diplodocus-dinosaur-in-europe/a-79277825?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paleontologists in Spain say they have found the first evidence of the long-necked Diplodocus genus of dinosaur outside of North America. They found bones at the rich La Tejeria fossil site in Teruel in eastern Spain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0de2aced0f2f29db69f0d97432fb05bd23c91d2d6d9d8b3b937abae13ae17f47</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the country's growing debt burden. And will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why AI researchers warn humanity could face extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e064b7d1d5fc1879b5b346a8a762e8a22fab5b5fa9035768374e6c8fb0bd941</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-ai-researchers-warn-humanity-could-face-extinction/a-79263146--d42b075a07d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-ai-researchers-warn-humanity-could-face-extinction/a-79263146?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Could artificial intelligence pose an existential threat to humanity? Some leading researchers are warning against an unregulated race toward AI superintelligence.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran and US: Two countries and the pistachio between them</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b03e988187b9762ccd1470000f27750d4e61877a460767da31c1132df1578878</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310--28756f33fc8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pistachios sold across the United States have a surprising history: California's trees trace their roots to Iran. Now, both regions face the same threat — their farmland is sinking as groundwater disappears.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's richest man Dangote's IPO out of reach in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cad65b8da9136d5333f1d4238a5c94ba45067de97129c5eb0cf8f5a29dac42ad</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398--03e0d1756308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The Crusades: How a medieval holy war still shapes politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07e5a92400e25efe8f4dc55b0b2a6b8ffb5e80c459e6ffd091872b40ac6f94d5</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784--8fa07b173177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1095, the Catholic Church launched the Crusades: wars that left millions dead and whose legacy still shapes political and ideological conflicts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Can Iran replace sea trade with land routes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:035a14e43b672d9e1126a2957672c4d85353dbb0286b31d5f6d23ba02b5a49f9</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179--9748aa6cdc36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran is shifting trade toward northern ports and land routes as its southern shipping faces a US blockade. Analysts say the corridors can keep essential goods moving, but cannot replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why are European banks moving gold out of United States?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38bee224cf6eaeaa8535e3ced72bfe7098fce4a101e6cf57e940d9fc5ffb27fa</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013--320ff1551fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Netherlands and France have moved their gold out of US vaults. Part of the reason is fears about the reliability of the US, but equally important is the need to keep gold closer to home in the event of a crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Corals as climate archive: Are El Nino events intensifying?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c430979a780de293d13934157af26311f2c5cc2b5b2c606de6de494dbd479569</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425--ac4752671640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Records show that El Nino events have been frequent and often extreme over the past few decades. Is this normal? Or is it the result of climate change? Corals can give us a clear indication.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e580c44fde12d615b40bcc18d822138371b8e7404bdf02cecb0d2fb6791afa4</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:01:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
